==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[rack one's brains]]
* [[wrack one's brain]]
* [[wrack one's brains]]

===Etymology===
Combination of ''[[rack]]'' (v), a medieval torture method, and ''[[brain]]'', thus meaning to cause the mind extreme discomfort.

===Verb===
'''[[rack]] one's [[brain]]'''

# {{idiomatic}} To [[struggle]] to [[think]] of or [[remember]] something.
#: ''I have been '''racking my brain''' all day trying to think of a birthday present for her.''

